From d59753b958254640cde149b7e367b346871a0790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:35:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(scss, stylus) highlight `from`/`to` keyframe selectors

CSS and Less scope the `from` / `to` keyframe selectors as
`selector-tag`, SCSS and Stylus left them plain (see the shared
css_consistency test). Add a shared KEYFRAME_POSITION mode to
lib/css-shared.js and use it in both grammars.

The mode only matches `from` / `to` as a whole word followed by `{`,
`,` or the end of the line, so `@for $i from 1 through 3`,
`linear-gradient(to right, ...)` and BEM/transition selectors such as
`&-leave-to {}` are not affected. Stylus indentation syntax (a bare
`from` / `to` line) is covered too.

Part of #4489

Assisted-by: Claude Code
